WEBVTT

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:12.820
All rounds have hit their targets.

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:16.430
It's not much of a feint,

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:18.880
but it's kind of the enemy to play along.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:21.520
Our forces are advancing on a different point.

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:24.420
If the enemy's going to split their main force, they'll send them there.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.520
An advance, huh?

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.170
I can't wait.

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:30.210
An attack on our forward base!

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:31.420
Initiate artillery strikes!

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:32.700
What?

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.580
The enemy is heading for our warning lines!

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:35.300
They're fast!

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.300
All forces prepare to intercept!

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.680
Send out the Trail Kriegers!

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:02.160
D-demons...

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:20.240
All enemy encampments have been destroyed.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.220
Proceeding to destroy the remaining enemies.

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:23.820
Roger.

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:02.030
It's time for Arandas-style calisthenics!

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:04.050
Another Mind
It's time for Arandas-style calisthenics!

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.290
Ready?
Another Mind

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:06.980
Attention!
Another Mind

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:07.020
Attention!

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:14.250
How many years has it been since I've done calisthenics?

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:18.760
I got a sketchbook and some crayons for doing them every day over summer break.

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:21.760
Want me to give you a stamp?

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:25.620
What are those guys doing? Are they kids?

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:28.220
They're taking it easy.

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:29.620
Too easy.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:30.810
We're at war!

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:33.840
Well, you know what we've all been through.

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:36.140
They can't stay tense forever.

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:38.990
You should relax a bit, too.

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:43.260
Are you really okay?

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:46.340
Yeah. It's just a system check today.

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:47.680
Not a real fight.

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:49.010
Go have fun.

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:51.040
Sorry to leave you behind.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:53.040
Not your fault, right?

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:57.830
Alrighty then! Private Portman is off to enjoy her vacation.

00:03:57.830 --> 00:03:59.430
Tokimune!

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:01.270
Oh, I'm being called.

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:02.050
See you.

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:07.430
Bye! I'll bring you a souvenir.

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:10.060
Okay, thanks!

00:04:13.450 --> 00:04:16.150
I just can't get used to it.

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:17.300
Get used to what?

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:19.800
We've been fighting all the time, right?

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:22.110
Like every single day.

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:26.950
But for the past few days, it's been so quiet here on the rear lines.

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:28.830
I'm bored, to be honest.

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:31.110
You should be glad to be bored.

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:34.580
It means no more episodes for you, and the Linkage Depth is stable, too.

00:04:34.930 --> 00:04:37.930
Well, I'd prefer not to fight, too, obviously.

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:39.530
But for some reason...

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:41.920
It's strange.

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:43.630
Strange?

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:48.130
It's sort of nostalgic, or a relief, or something.

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:50.220
Anyway, I'm just bored.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:53.780
Yeah, it might be the first time in a while.

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:56.860
Tokimune, start it up.

00:04:56.860 --> 00:04:57.590
Sure.

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:05.110
This'll be over soon.

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:07.320
I'm just getting the data ready to send to HQ.

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:08.570
Okay.

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:16.010
Jamie?

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:19.180
In the end...

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:20.870
What am I doing?

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:22.380
You're working, aren't you?

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:24.090
No, I mean...

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:31.140
In the end, I still don't know what Argevollen is.

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:33.860
It's not just you.

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:36.940
Neither do I, and neither does anybody else.

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:37.900
We're all the same.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:42.330
But I've been working with Argevollen since the beginning.

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:43.580
And still...

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:48.280
I still can't understand how hard things are for you.

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:50.610
You're doing a good job, Jamie.

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:52.540
That's what your job is, right?

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:54.670
That's why I can fight.

00:05:57.220 --> 00:05:59.410
I just meant what I said, okay?

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:00.820
Right, right.

00:06:00.820 --> 00:06:01.960
Just what you said.

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:02.880
Just what you said!

00:06:03.310 --> 00:06:06.690
You're doing your job just fine, Jamie-kun.

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:09.140
Suguro-san!

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:11.460
Hello, you two.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.270
What? You're not supporting Argevollen anymore?

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:20.380
Well, that may not be the best way to put it.

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:23.740
But we've made it so you and the local mechanics

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:28.280
can maintain the system, the motors, and everything else.

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:30.660
That was the primary purpose of this.

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:35.650
You're all talented people and better able to deal with it

00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:37.910
than our own staff, I think.

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:40.540
Talented, huh?

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:41.670
Yeah, right.

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:44.890
But is it okay?

00:06:45.690 --> 00:06:49.200
Even if we can all maintain Arge now...

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:50.180
What about Tokimune?

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:54.260
That'll be <i>fine!</i>

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:58.940
Suguro-san, why don't we discuss the rest over here?

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:01.130
That's right.

00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:04.920
I need to talk to you, too, Captain Suzushiro.

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:10.030
Even with the mass-produced models out there,

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:13.620
Argevollen is still an important part of our company.

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:17.500
I'd like you to continue gathering data like you have been.

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:22.640
I'm aware that the Perphevollens have been seeing great results.

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:24.500
Why are you still concerned with Argevollen?

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:27.560
It's true that Tokimune-kun's efforts

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:29.780
gave us the data we needed for the mass-produced models.

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:30.510
But...

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:37.140
The mass-produced models and Argevollen don't share the exact same system.

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:39.520
They don't?

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:44.040
As you know, Argevollen requires Jamie-kun for system authorization,

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:47.530
and Tokimune-kun for activation.

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:49.610
Why does that matter?

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:51.820
And perhaps for that reason,

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:56.060
there is a type of noise in Argevollen's systems.

00:07:56.900 --> 00:07:58.130
Noise?

00:07:58.130 --> 00:08:03.460
It's possible that this noise is what's keeping Tokimune-kun safe.

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:08.250
We need more data from Argevollen to make sure.

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:10.180
Wait a second.

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:14.000
You just said he was safe, and now it's just "possible"?

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:16.470
And why are you just telling us about this now?

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:19.350
Last time I asked, you didn't say a word about this!

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:21.600
It was confidential.

00:08:21.970 --> 00:08:23.860
Some kind of new research?

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:25.440
Using Argevollen?

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:26.770
That's right.

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:29.870
It's a good thing for you all, isn't it?

00:08:29.870 --> 00:08:35.280
Continuing to pilot Argevollen is what's best for Tokimune-kun's future.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:36.630
Future?

00:08:36.630 --> 00:08:37.490
Um...

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:38.850
What?

00:08:39.850 --> 00:08:44.730
It's Captain Samonji who's actually commanding the Perphevollens, right?

00:08:44.730 --> 00:08:45.970
That's right.

00:08:45.970 --> 00:08:47.630
You knew that, didn't you?

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:52.640
No, I've never actually seen it.

00:08:52.640 --> 00:08:54.240
How is the captain...

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:55.630
I mean Lieutenant Samonji?

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:57.140
He's doing fine.

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:59.260
He's doing a wonderful job as commander.

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:04.510
He's controlling whole formations of the unmanned Perphevollens.

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:07.650
He was grateful to you, too.

00:09:09.620 --> 00:09:10.650
I see.

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:15.820
Tokimune...

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:19.200
Man, what the heck is this?

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:21.740
We're not important now that there's a new model?

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:23.860
We have to do our own maintenance?

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:25.580
This is totally a demotion!

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:27.280
Isn't it a good thing?

00:09:27.280 --> 00:09:29.820
In a sense, things are more normal now.

00:09:29.820 --> 00:09:33.860
Now we can help you maintain Arge.

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:36.500
Well, that's true, but...

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:40.470
A new model isn't always a better one.

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:42.370
A good mech

00:09:42.370 --> 00:09:45.350
is something that needs to be raised by a good pilot and good mechanics.

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:47.980
From now on, you and Tokimune

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:52.230
must make Argevollen into a machine that's unique to you.

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:53.720
Wow.

00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:56.020
The chief just said something really cool.

00:09:56.020 --> 00:09:58.030
All he does to us is yell.

00:09:58.030 --> 00:09:59.490
We're treated too differently!

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:01.490
You guys don't need it.

00:10:01.490 --> 00:10:03.870
This is a new beginning for this thing.

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:05.870
Well, that's true.

00:10:06.280 --> 00:10:10.390
Alright, time to start showing you the ropes, Jamie the newbie!

00:10:10.390 --> 00:10:11.880
Yeah, thanks!

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:13.730
Oh, right.

00:10:13.730 --> 00:10:15.520
This should be okay now.

00:10:15.520 --> 00:10:17.290
It's Argevollen's manual.

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:18.480
Manual?

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:19.310
Yeah.

00:10:19.310 --> 00:10:24.010
I can download the detailed manual for Argevollen that I couldn't see before, I'm told.

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:28.090
So we can finally learn the secrets of Argevollen!

00:10:28.090 --> 00:10:30.900
Black box! Black box!

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:34.900
The new power of the United Kingdom of Arandas,

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:38.900
the latest Trail Kriegers, the Perphevollen strike force.

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:41.910
The Perphevollens have been destroying the enemies

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:44.950
on one battlefield after another.

00:10:44.950 --> 00:10:47.070
Our force's victory is near.

00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:53.710
Hey, Tokimune.

00:10:54.190 --> 00:10:55.000
Yes?

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.460
Come with me.

00:10:58.410 --> 00:11:00.240
This is not good.

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:02.540
Yes, not good at all.

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:06.970
I can just imagine how arrogant Cayenne is getting.

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:11.810
What we need now is not thoughtless hatred of the enemy.

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:16.850
As you said, the capital is already working toward peace.

00:11:16.850 --> 00:11:19.820
The Perphevollens are in the way.

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:21.470
Shall we crush them?

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:31.780
With everyone evacuating, all my favorite bars are closing.

00:11:31.780 --> 00:11:33.080
It really sucks.

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:39.320
You may be winning, but the citizens aren't hiding what they think.

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:41.220
They're tired of war.

00:11:44.190 --> 00:11:47.770
Have you seen the 8th Unit since then?

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:48.470
No.

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:10.040
I'm sorry, did I ruin a beautiful friendship?

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:11.000
It's fine.

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:14.000
You're no fun.

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:26.060
Okui-san, I haven't been drinking since that happened...

00:12:26.060 --> 00:12:28.320
Shut up. Just keep me company.

00:12:28.320 --> 00:12:30.480
Bartender, gin and milk.

00:12:33.460 --> 00:12:35.610
Isn't it unwise to be drinking this early?

00:12:35.610 --> 00:12:37.220
It's fine.

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:41.690
So what do you think?

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:44.440
About Captain Samonji.

00:12:44.440 --> 00:12:47.120
It's been two months since he up and left us.

00:12:49.130 --> 00:12:51.470
We're all grown-ups.

00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:54.470
Nobody's said anything since the day he left.

00:12:54.470 --> 00:12:57.780
Tanita-san, Koshikawa, Kutsuwada...

00:12:57.780 --> 00:12:59.640
Even that idiot Yamanami.

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:02.650
A promotion's a good thing, sure.

00:13:02.650 --> 00:13:07.760
It's a waste for a great captain like him to run a unit like this.

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:09.480
That's what I thought.

00:13:09.480 --> 00:13:13.190
But I was proud of him, too.

00:13:13.190 --> 00:13:14.650
Proud...

00:13:15.020 --> 00:13:17.750
I survived because I fought with him.

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:19.820
I was able to fulfill my mission, too.

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:23.560
That mission where he and the executive officer were gone and I was in command...

00:13:24.460 --> 00:13:27.180
If it hadn't been for you, we'd have been wiped out.

00:13:29.020 --> 00:13:30.220
That's not true...

00:13:30.220 --> 00:13:31.460
It is!

00:13:33.020 --> 00:13:35.300
Thank you.

00:13:35.720 --> 00:13:42.070
That's why I realized that I'm... We're only still alive because of him.

00:13:42.070 --> 00:13:44.310
And yet he said goodbye without a word!

00:13:44.310 --> 00:13:47.310
No, he didn't even say goodbye.

00:13:47.310 --> 00:13:49.420
Yeah, that's right!

00:13:49.420 --> 00:13:53.110
Hey, why are you guys drinking so early in the day?

00:13:55.110 --> 00:13:56.530
What are you guys doing here?

00:13:56.530 --> 00:13:59.690
Hey, Tokimune. Jamie-chan was looking for you.

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:01.780
Leave this to us and go back to base.

00:14:01.780 --> 00:14:03.150
Jamie was?

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:04.500
Okay.

00:14:05.660 --> 00:14:08.170
Hey, I'm not done talking!

00:14:08.170 --> 00:14:09.670
Yeah, yeah.

00:14:09.670 --> 00:14:12.030
You can talk to us instead.

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:14.000
Now let's drink.

00:14:16.270 --> 00:14:18.760
What are you all doing?

00:14:18.760 --> 00:14:20.530
It's the stud.

00:14:20.530 --> 00:14:23.300
Weren't you eating lunch with Silfy-san and that other girl?

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:24.770
Yeah,

00:14:24.770 --> 00:14:29.310
the two girls went off shopping and the guy comes home alone.

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:31.140
And that's why you're here?

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:33.810
You really are a dedicated pilot!

00:14:34.250 --> 00:14:36.420
Aren't you glad, Akane?

00:14:36.420 --> 00:14:37.320
I guess.

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:40.950
So, as you were saying...

00:14:40.950 --> 00:14:43.740
Jamie's inside Argevollen.

00:14:43.740 --> 00:14:44.830
What?

00:14:44.830 --> 00:14:48.740
The new manual explains how to do a system check.

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:49.830
She's trying it out.

00:14:50.180 --> 00:14:51.130
Yup.

00:14:51.130 --> 00:14:54.030
With this, I can see what level we're at.

00:14:54.030 --> 00:14:56.290
Tokimune's not here, but I'll try it.

00:14:56.690 --> 00:14:58.290
Jamie Hazaford.

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:01.390
ID Number 06120530.

00:15:02.260 --> 00:15:03.300
Dive.

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:11.300
Arge's booted up?

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:17.060
System check in this mode

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:21.330
is visualized to allow for early detection of damaged or abnormal data.

00:15:21.330 --> 00:15:24.950
A simplified brain projection system has been achieved...

00:15:24.950 --> 00:15:26.200
What does that mean?

00:15:32.940 --> 00:15:35.170
What is that?

00:15:35.770 --> 00:15:37.200
What?

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:38.540
What is this?

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:41.930
They're closed, but I can see...

00:15:48.950 --> 00:15:50.520
What is this?

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:03.820
Jamie! What's wrong?

00:16:03.820 --> 00:16:04.740
Jamie-chan!

00:16:04.740 --> 00:16:07.050
Jamie!

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:19.130
Jamie...

00:16:21.050 --> 00:16:22.380
Tokimune...

00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:25.860
That was really bad.

00:16:25.860 --> 00:16:28.740
You weren't coming out, so I opened Arge,

00:16:28.740 --> 00:16:30.180
and you were unconscious.

00:16:33.820 --> 00:16:38.210
I saw the U-Link system.

00:16:38.820 --> 00:16:39.750
You saw it?

00:16:40.690 --> 00:16:42.860
Sort of...

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:44.380
Inside my head.

00:16:44.380 --> 00:16:45.460
Yeah.

00:16:45.460 --> 00:16:47.960
Is that what's it like for you?

00:16:47.960 --> 00:16:50.660
I don't know what you saw,

00:16:51.220 --> 00:16:52.700
but that's probably it.

00:17:04.760 --> 00:17:08.970
You know, I wonder where the Perphevollens are going.

00:17:08.970 --> 00:17:11.460
It's got nothing to do with us.

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:13.760
That stinks. It's like we're being left out.

00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:15.560
I'm fine with being left out.

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:21.190
You guys...

00:17:21.550 --> 00:17:24.940
Hey, guys. It's not even evening yet.

00:17:24.940 --> 00:17:26.670
Nah, nah...

00:17:26.670 --> 00:17:28.660
What are you gals doing here, then?

00:17:28.660 --> 00:17:30.570
Oh, you know.

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:35.330
Man, gimme a break...

00:17:35.680 --> 00:17:39.340
Tanita-san is being all philosophical about it.

00:17:39.340 --> 00:17:42.340
But I understand why he's so sad.

00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:47.140
I've always thought I didn't care what other people did.

00:17:47.140 --> 00:17:49.640
But this really bothers me.

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:54.760
It means you guys really are part of the 8th Unit.

00:17:55.850 --> 00:17:57.350
Maybe.

00:17:58.030 --> 00:18:01.600
I wonder what Samonji-san is doing now.

00:18:04.880 --> 00:18:09.480
As you can see, the new Trail Kriegers' performance has been incredible.

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:13.240
Our forces are gradually regaining ground.

00:18:16.180 --> 00:18:18.500
Taking the credit from somebody else, huh?

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:21.250
However!

00:18:21.250 --> 00:18:25.180
Trail Krieger units alone won't change the war!

00:18:25.180 --> 00:18:28.260
The military should take a broader view.

00:18:28.820 --> 00:18:33.760
We need the Perphevollens to restore the citizens' trust in the military.

00:18:33.760 --> 00:18:36.260
But that's all.

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:38.640
That was a really boring meeting.

00:18:39.270 --> 00:18:40.520
Just a pep rally...

00:18:42.780 --> 00:18:45.690
The old men are trying to protect themselves.

00:18:47.840 --> 00:18:50.020
The path to peace, huh?

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:54.530
But "peace" is nothing more than an excuse for surrender used by politicians.

00:18:55.670 --> 00:18:58.420
Somehow it's the opposite of usual.

00:18:59.060 --> 00:18:59.910
Yeah?

00:19:00.340 --> 00:19:01.950
I was hoping

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:06.660
I could understand how you feel when you pilot it,

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:08.420
at least a little, but...

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:11.810
It made me feel sick.

00:19:13.410 --> 00:19:16.500
What I saw and what I was thinking came together in my head...

00:19:16.500 --> 00:19:19.930
I didn't know what was me and what was outside.

00:19:21.150 --> 00:19:24.060
I thought that this must be it.

00:19:24.060 --> 00:19:27.710
This must be what you were talking about.

00:19:27.710 --> 00:19:32.030
I don't know how scary fighting is because I just watch from the sidelines.

00:19:32.740 --> 00:19:37.060
But is this how Arge's systems are?

00:19:37.060 --> 00:19:39.090
They're this terrible?

00:19:39.840 --> 00:19:43.370
I've been making you pilot that thing...

00:19:44.390 --> 00:19:45.040
I'm sorry...

00:19:45.960 --> 00:19:46.960
I'm sorry.

00:19:49.060 --> 00:19:52.180
You were caught up in this, too, weren't you?

00:19:52.180 --> 00:19:54.860
You're a civilian, but you've been through all that scary stuff.

00:19:55.690 --> 00:19:58.970
And I'm glad I got to pilot Arge.

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:03.830
I was new, and useless,

00:20:03.830 --> 00:20:07.060
but thanks to Arge, I was able to fight with everyone.

00:20:07.060 --> 00:20:10.980
I love the 8th Unit.

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:12.990
I've come to love it.

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:15.990
Come to...

00:20:15.990 --> 00:20:17.570
It's strange, isn't it?

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:19.190
Even though I'm fighting...

00:20:19.190 --> 00:20:21.830
Even though I'm at war, I'm relieved.

00:20:23.410 --> 00:20:26.000
I can fight because everyone is with me.

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:28.500
Everyone, including you.

00:20:30.420 --> 00:20:31.500
Thank you.

00:20:38.520 --> 00:20:39.870
Oh, crap.

00:20:40.470 --> 00:20:41.530
What's wrong?

00:20:41.530 --> 00:20:42.340
Is it crowded?

00:20:43.520 --> 00:20:45.640
Oh, Lorenz-san!

00:20:47.500 --> 00:20:48.910
You two...

00:20:48.910 --> 00:20:51.610
You finally seduced her, huh, sexy boy?

00:20:51.610 --> 00:20:53.940
No...

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:55.650
Okay, so, everyone...

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:57.190
Hey, come over here.

00:20:57.190 --> 00:20:58.820
Tell us the details.

00:21:01.300 --> 00:21:04.000
He's out there fighting, even now.

00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:06.330
It's quite moving.

00:21:06.330 --> 00:21:09.600
By all rights he should have died,

00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:11.540
but he's still living.

00:21:11.540 --> 00:21:17.180
Well, finding out why is the reason Argevollen exists.

00:21:17.180 --> 00:21:19.180
So whether he lives or dies,

00:21:19.180 --> 00:21:21.300
he's useful to you, huh?

00:21:23.060 --> 00:21:28.690
You don't think he's doing his best for his country, and his unit?

00:21:39.120 --> 00:21:42.010
The supply trucks are coming in all the time.

00:21:42.010 --> 00:21:44.580
We'll begin the mission soon.

00:21:44.580 --> 00:21:47.720
I'd heard Richthofen would be back.

00:21:47.720 --> 00:21:51.840
He's recovered, so he wants to participate in the invasion.

00:21:52.310 --> 00:21:56.840
It looks like the Silver Will really has a hold on him.

00:21:59.930 --> 00:22:13.230
We gaze into each other's eyes, open our hearts.

00:22:13.230 --> 00:22:19.450
A cycle of strength and weakness.

00:22:19.450 --> 00:22:26.080
Your eyes must have adjusted somewhat.

00:22:26.080 --> 00:22:32.750
Verbalize though I may,

00:22:32.750 --> 00:22:40.550
I remember that I can't

00:22:40.550 --> 00:22:47.180
rationalize everything

00:22:47.180 --> 00:22:54.360
The world will change, as long as I remain courageous.

00:22:55.610 --> 00:23:02.360
The telepathy I wouldn't have discovered alone,

00:23:02.360 --> 00:23:08.490
leads me ahead, behind your dazzling silouette.

00:23:08.490 --> 00:23:15.880
But even so, I'll keep my unwavering gaze on you;

00:23:15.880 --> 00:23:22.470
It'll reach you someday.

00:23:36.310 --> 00:23:38.070
Disturbance

00:23:38.070 --> 00:23:39.280
"Disturbance."
Disturbance
